#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""waddle mesh: the mesh network of LilyGO T5 units (up to 32 members).

  waddle mesh new-unit [gateway] [--pr N] [--port P] [file.bin]
                         put WaddleOS on a new unit (or the gateway) over USB,
                         then check that it works
  waddle mesh setup      make the network (the first time) and add your own
                         units on this Wi-Fi straight away
  waddle mesh invite NAME
                         a link for someone new, to send by Signal
  waddle mesh join LINK [--name N]
                         (the newcomer) join with that link: your unit on
                         File Transfer -> Join a Network
  waddle mesh approve    let in those who asked to join
  waddle mesh remove NAME
                         take someone out of the network
  waddle mesh members    who is in the network
  waddle mesh check      ask every unit set up here how it is (--logs: its last log lines too)
  waddle mesh server [--pr N]
                         update the Pi server over SSH and check it came back

The admin's keys stay on this computer (~/.config/waddle/admin.json). Each unit
made its own keys on first start; its private key never leaves it. The Pi only
passes on sealed packets. Uses only the Python standard library.
"""

